          "path": "_m/g/c/w/2/national-football-museum-wp/photo-original-hand-wr.jpg",
          "filename": "Original laws of the game 1863.jpg",
          "caption": "Photo of the original hand written 'Laws of the game' for association Football drafted for and behalf of The Football Association by Ebenezer Cobb Morley in 1863 on display at the National Football Museum, Manchester. The handwriting on the left is that of Cobb Morley and reads:\nMeeting 24th November 1863\nFreemasons Tavern\nThe minutes of the meeting held 17th Nov were read and confirmed.\nLetters from\nMr StewardThe Captain of Football at Shrewsbury School\nThe Rev J C Thring\nLt H C Moore\nMr Chambers\nand Mr J Bell \nwere read\n\nThe Secretary laid before the meeting the (illegible, but probably ‘rules’) which had been drawn up in (illegible, but probably ‘pursuance’) of the (illegible) at previous meetings which were as follows",
          "alt": "Photo of the original hand written 'Laws of the game' for association Football drafted for and behalf of The Football Association by Ebenezer Cobb Morley in 1863 on display at the National Football Museum, Manchester. The handwriting on the left is that of Cobb Morley and reads:\nMeeting 24th November 1863\nFreemasons Tavern\nThe minutes of the meeting held 17th Nov were read and confirmed.\nLetters from\nMr StewardThe Captain of Football at Shrewsbury School\nThe Rev J C Thring\nLt H C Moore\nMr Chambers\nand Mr J Bell \nwere read\n\nThe Secretary laid before the meeting the (illegible, but probably ‘rules’) which had been drawn up in (illegible, but probably ‘pursuance’) of the (illegible) at previous meetings which were as follows",
          "width": 1600,
          "height": 1200,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
          "artist": "Adrian Roebuck",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Original_laws_of_the_game_1863.jpg",
          "sourceType": "core",
          "sourceArticleId": "national-football-museum-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "gcw2"
